dsh-usage-limits launchpad-status: show plugin status contributions on the Launchpad (dsh-TUI 0.15.0).

dsh-TUI 0.15.0 renders `ctx.tuiStatus` text entries and rich views (registerView, the frozen
`tui.dsh/v1alpha1` status-line seam XI) only in Chat, above the prompt. The Launchpad (first screen)
is a separate component and shows none, so a status line appears only after the first prompt. Chat
now passes its status entries, views, the pointer-only view kit and the view error reporter to the
Launchpad, which renders them the same way (rich views inside PluginStatusViewBoundary, then the
joined dim text) in one full-width, centred block above the input card. The layout budgets the
block's rows, the block yields first when rows run short, and the input card never shrinks.

Applies to stock nix-dsh dsh-tui 0.15.0 (after its preset-schedule-deny fix) on its own and in the
fleet order (keybindings, alt, model-selector, usage-limits, speed, incognito).
Source: https://github.com/jakehemmerle/dsh-usage-limits (nix/tui-patch.nix).

